      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] If the input path is a non-regular file (e.g. `/dev/null` or a named pipe), `file.tellg()` will return `-1`. Casting this to `size_t` results in `SIZE_MAX`, causing `data.resize()` to throw a fatal `std::bad_alloc` exception.\n\nConsider checking for `-1` to handle non-regular files gracefully:\n```cpp\n\tstd::streampos pos \u003d file.tellg();\n\tif (pos \u003c 0) {\n\t\tfprintf(stderr, \"Error: cannot determine file size for \u0027%s\u0027\\n\", path.c_str());\n\t\treturn false;\n\t}\n\tsize_t size \u003d static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(pos);\n\tfile.seekg(0, std::ios::beg);\n\n\tdata.resize(size);\n``` [🔗](http://go/tj/8ddb0f15-ffe5-40ce-ba75-387ce4dc165f)",
